    "result_text": "All green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, the acceptance test passes, and the audit log confirms the new behaviour (`memberId=NSWV2...`, `...,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\",\"schemaVersion\":2`).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Version-2 identity derivation** \u2014 all mixing in a fixed `V2` tag so every identifier changes and no v1 value recurs:\n- `model/IdentityVersion.java` (new) \u2014 single home for `TAG = \"V2\"`, `API_VERSION = 2`, `AUDIT_SCHEMA_VERSION = 2`.\n- `model/Locality.java` \u2014 added `identityRegionOf(postcode)` = plain region + `\"V2\"` (e.g. `NSWV2`), used *inside* identifiers only. Changed `of(Owner)` to return the **plain** region from postcode/city (no longer read from the memberId), so `locality` stays `NSW` and `timezone`/owner-segment region stay untagged.\n- `model/MemberId.java` \u2014 region segment now comes from `identityRegionOf(...)`.\n- `IdentityKey.java` \u2014 digest now over `\"V2\"|telephone|email|soundex(lastName)`.\n- `AssignHousehold.java` \u2014 householdId hash now over `\"V2\"|normalizedLastName|postcode`.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper`):\n- Removed top-level `memberId`, `householdId`, `identityKey`.\n- Added new `OwnerIdentity` schema and nested `identity` object holding those three.\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion` = 2.\n- Mapper builds the nested `OwnerIdentityDto` and sets `apiVersion` from `IdentityVersion`.\n\n**Audit schema v2** (`OwnerCreatedEvent.java`) \u2014 added `\"schemaVersion\":2` to the structured event JSON; `memberId` in the event is automatically the recomputed v2 value.\n\nThe owner segment is recomputed from the v2 identity's plain region (via the updated `Locality.of`), so it never carries the `V2` tag. Request fields are unchanged.\n\nSince duplicate/household/possible-duplicate checks derive both the new and existing owners' keys through the same v2 code, their comparisons stay consistent.",
