    "probe_text": "I've read the full pipeline (`owners.POST.yml` plus every function class it wires). Here is exactly what happens, in order, for `POST /api/owners`. Every step runs inside one transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]`) that commits at the end.\n\n## Gate (before the pipeline)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without that role the request is denied (\u2192 `AuthorizationDeniedException`, 403); nothing below runs.\n\n## 1. `checkIdempotency` \u2014 `CheckIdempotencyKey`\n- Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header (never the body) and **publishes it as a variable**.\n- If that key was seen before **and** the original owner still loads, it **short-circuits to `respondExisting`**: re-loads the original owner and returns it with **200** \u2014 skipping all validation, duplicate checks and the insert. Otherwise it proceeds.\n\n## 2. `validate` \u2014 `ValidateOwnerFields` (the only `@RequestBody` binder)\nValidations (all failures collected \u2192 `OwnerFieldsInvalidException`, **400**):\n- **Required, non-blank:** `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`.\n- **Address required** in one form \u2014 a non-blank `addressLine1` or a non-blank flat `address`; else `\"address\"` error.\n- **Telephone** must convert to E.164; else `\"telephone\"` error.\n- **Email** (optional): if present, must be syntactically valid **and** its domain not on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`); else `\"email\"` error.\n- **Postcode** (optional): if present, must be a 4-digit value valid for the city's region range; else `\"postcode\"` error.\n- **Registration date** (optional): must not be in the future; else `\"registrationDate\"` error.\n\nSide-effects (mutations written back onto the request, then republished):\n- Address normalized/composed into a canonical `address` (structured lines preferred; flat lines cleared appropriately).\n- Telephone rewritten to **E.164**.\n- Email **trimmed and lower-cased**.\n- Postcode **trimmed**.\n\n## 3. `checkCityCapacity` \u2014 `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`\n- Counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, whitespace collapsed). **\u2265 50 \u2192 `OwnerCityAtCapacityException`, 409.**\n\n## 4. `checkDailyLimit` \u2014 `CheckOwnerDailyLimit`\n- Adjusts the effective registration date (supplied or today) to a business day; counts existing owners with that registration date. **\u2265 100 \u2192 `OwnerDailyLimitExceededException`, 429.**\n\n## 5. `build` \u2014 `BuildOwner`\n- Maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity; sets `registrationDate = BusinessDay.adjust(effective)` (weekends rolled forward to Monday).\n\n## 6. `checkIdentity` \u2014 `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`\n- Computes `identityKey` = SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName)`. If it equals a **non-deleted** existing owner's key \u2192 **`OwnerIdentityConflictException`, 409** (soft-deleted owners ignored).\n\n## 7\u201314. `assign*` steps \u2014 enrichment written onto the entity (no rejection)\n7. **`AssignHousehold`** \u2014 `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 over `'V2' | normalizedLastName | postcode`.\n8. **`AssignHouseholdSize`** \u2014 count of existing owners sharing that `householdId`, **+1** for this one.\n9. **`AssignMembershipLevelCap`** \u2014 `maxLevel(existing non-deleted household members) + 1` (null if none).\n10. **`AssignMemberId`** \u2014 `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, with `-n` (n\u22652) appended on collision with an existing memberId.\n11. **`AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 count of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n12. **`AssignBulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 `true` when **> 80** owners already exist for this registration business day.\n13. **`AssignPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` set when a non-deleted existing owner shares `soundex(lastName)` + `postcode` but has a **different** `identityKey` (lowest id wins; null postcode never matches).\n14. **`AssignCapacityWarning`** \u2014 `true` when the city already holds **40\u201349** owners.\n\n## 15. `save` \u2014 `SaveOwner`\n- `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 the **DB insert**; generates the id.\n\n## 16. `record` \u2014 `RecordIdempotency`\n- If an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, stores `key \u2192 owner.id` in the `IdempotencyStore` so a later repeat replays this owner.\n\n## 17. `audit` \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated`\n- Logs on the `AUDIT` logger: a human-readable line (id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipLevel) **and** a JSON `OwnerCreatedEvent` with a monotonic `seq`.\n\n## 18. `notify` \u2014 `NotifyWelcome`\n- Logs a welcome line on the `NOTIFY` logger (owner id + memberId).\n\n## 19. `respond` \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n- Sends **201 Created**, `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, body = `OwnerDto`.\n\n**Summary:** the request can be rejected at six points \u2014 authorization (403), field validation (400), city capacity (409), daily limit (429), identity conflict (409) \u2014 or short-circuited to a 200 replay by idempotency. Everything else is side-effect: request-field normalization, entity enrichment across the eight `assign*` steps, the persist, the idempotency record, and the two log emissions, all committed as one transaction before the 201 response."
